<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cornplanter</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1750–<a href="/years/1836">1836</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Gaiant'wake</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cornplanter was a Seneca war chief who fought on the British side in the American War of Independence and later sought peace with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. He took part in the treaties of the 1780s and 1790s and was granted land in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a>, where his descendants lived until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kinzua-dam">Kinzua Dam</a> flooded it. He was a half-brother of the prophet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/handsome-lake">Handsome Lake</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cornplanter.jpg" alt="Cornplanter" width="320" height="387" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: F. Bartoli · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cornplanter.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
